      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(clickclack): wrap websocket message rejections with Error for diagnostics",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe websocket message handler in ClickClack's gateway uses `.catch(reject)` to\nforward errors from the async message processor. When the processor throws a\nnon-Error value, the raw rejection loses the stack trace and makes downstream\nerror diagnostics unreliable.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nReplace `.catch(reject)` with an explicit catch block that preserves Error\ninstances and wraps non-Error values with the original value visible in the\nError message and preserved as `cause`.\n\n## Evidence\n\nGateway tests pass, including the new non-Error rejection test:\n\n```text\n$ pnpm test extensions/clickclack/src/gateway.test.ts\n\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  6 passed (6)\n   ✓ wraps non-Error ws message rejections with the original value in the message\n```\n\nThe patched catch path at `gateway.ts:209`:\n\n```typescript\n.catch((e: unknown) =>\n  reject(\n    e instanceof Error\n      ? e\n      : new Error(`ClickClack ws message failed: ${String(e)}`, { cause: e }),\n  ),\n);\n```\n\nAI-assisted: built with Codex\n",
        "branch": "sunlit/fix/clickclack-rejection",
